window.products.push({"id":149375,"name":"WR60X10141 Evaporator Fan Motor Refrigerator Part WR60X31522 WR60X23584 WR60X28783 WR60X10346 WR60X10046 WR60X10138 WR60X28784 Model A3316ABSARBB HTS1","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61BC7ulh5iS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Ge Evaporator Fan Motor Wr60x10141 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers WR60X23584, AP5955766, WR60X10346, PS10063450, WR60X10045, WR60X10046, WR60X10072, WR60X10138, WR60X27646. Refrigerator Fan Motor Wr60x10141 is compatible with General Electric, Hotpoint appliance's. It is located at the back of the freezer and operates on 115 volts and 60Hz. It fits hundreds of models, so it's essential to ensure that the replacement part is compatible with your special refrigerator model. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the Wr60x10141 Evaporator Fan Replacement Part? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Ge Wr60x10141 Refrigerator Evaporator Fan Motor will help if your appliance is noisy, fridge is too warm, freezer section is too warm, or it doesn't start. Before attempting to repair the motor, make sure to disconnect the power to the appliance. 💡 The Wr60x10141 Fan Motor is a crucial component of a refrigerator's cooling system. Wr60x10141 Refrigerator Evaporator Fan Motor Replacement is a small electric motor that rotates the fan blades. Ge Evap Fan Motor Wr60x10141 is responsible for circulating air over the refrigerator coils, which convert heat into cool air. Wr60X10141 Evaporator Fan Motor meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 Will fridge work without evaporator fan? In most cases, a fridge will still work without an evaporator fan, but it may not work as efficiently as it should. The evaporator fan helps circulate the cold air throughout the refrigerator, so without it, the temperature may not be consistent, and there may be hot spots or cold spots in different areas of the fridge. The lack of airflow can cause frost/ice buildup on the evaporator coil, which can eventually lead to other problems with the fridge. 💡 What happens if evaporator fan stops? If the evaporator fan stops working, the refrigerator's cooling system may not function correctly, and several problems can occur. Firstly, without the evaporator fan, the cold air will not circulate properly throughout the fridge, causing temperature inconsistencies. Secondly, the refrigerator may make unusual noises or stop running altogether if the evaporator fan is not working correctly. Check your Evaporator Motor regulary to prevent further damage.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61BC7ulh5iS._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07L13NSPC","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-149375","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07L13NSPC","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07L13NSPC","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
