window.products.push({"id":149464,"name":"WR55X10025 Temperature Sensor Refrigerator Thermistor PS304103 AP3185407 General Electric WR55X11152 Ultra Durable Part Number WR50X10067 GSH25JFXBBB ","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":6.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41ELISSCLmS._SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Thermistor WR55X10025 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP3185407, 914093, AH304103, EA304103, PS304103, WR50X10027, WR50X10034, WR50X10055, WR50X10067, WR55X10025B, WR55X10026, WR55X10027, WR55X10028, WR55X10030, WR55X10087, WR55X10088, WR55X10089, WR55X10367, WR55X10380, WR55X10661, WR55X10711, WR55X10735, WR55X10736, WR55X10737, WR55X10937, WR55X10938, WR55X10939, WR55X11121, WR55X11141, WR55X11151, WR55X11152. It is compatible with GE and Hotpoint appliances. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the Ge Temperature Sensor Wr55x10025? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. General Electric Wr55x10025 Refrigerator Temperature Sensor, will help if your appliance is too warm, freezer section is too warm, fridge is too cold, or freezer is not defrosting. Ge Thermistor Wr55x10025 fits hundreds of models and can be installed in a few minutes. 💡 The Refrigerator Thermistor Wr55x10025 is responsible for monitoring the temperature inside the refrigerator and transmitting the information to the thermostat, which regulates the cooling process to maintain a consistent temperature. The sensor is typically located at the back of the refrigerator or in the freezer compartment. Ge Wr55x10025 Thermistor meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡 How do you test a temperature sensor on a GE refrigerator? To test a temperature sensor on a GE refrigerator, you should locate the sensor, disconnect the power, remove the sensor, and test it using a multimeter. The multimeter should measure resistance within the specified range, indicating that the sensor is working properly. If the sensor is faulty, you will need to replace it with a new one and reinstall it in its original position. 💡 How long should a temperature sensor last? The lifespan of a temperature sensor in a refrigerator can vary depending on the make and model of the refrigerator and how often it is used. However, a temperature sensor in a refrigerator can generally last for several years, up to a decade or more, before it needs to be replaced. Factors such as environmental conditions, such as temperature and humidity, can also impact the lifespan of a temperature sensor.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41ELISSCLmS._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07VW82TZ4","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-149464","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07VW82TZ4","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07VW82TZ4","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
